{7} \\div 3 = \\dfrac{5}{21}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142718 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2208" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142718 #edb/ref 1071 "What picture is missing from the division model below?\n\n![](images/bb/bb9bf65df4eb34dac86c30479de00123c796c82d3137b69d20a1d21eecae67c3.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142718 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "386c19cf-1f88-551b-b1bc-6f4baa142d2a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142718 #edb/ref 1074 "In the model, we have $\\dfrac{4}{6}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to divide by $\\color{blue}2$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}2$ equal parts horizontally. \n\n![](images/84/84f5fc54aa28636fd587cc712d039bdb984edec3dc3f5f22f891dbc1776fbd3e.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{4}{12}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore, the missing picture is the following:\n\n![](images/a6/a68a88f55f3f06c1f238927ae53df6a64348e2ab190673e445568cd1161d46c7.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142719 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2209" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142719 #edb/ref 1071 "What number is missing from the division problem below?\n\n![](images/0b/0b119e18348ad6f0ee31f2ad3e57cad4fc66403302df5590a8526ce39e930c78.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142719 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e85814d8-b93e-573e-aca5-2c64e601d05a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142719 #edb/ref 1074 "We have $\\dfrac{3}{4}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{3}{20}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/eb/eb114471d69ebd728a176b521ab410ab2b16d2bccc039e003faacd9c5d445e96.png)\n\nThe division operation splits each vertical line into $\\color{blue}5$ equal parts. So the shaded parts on the left are $\\color{blue}5$ times larger than the shaded parts on the right. \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 3 4 \\div {\\color{blue}{5}} = \\dfrac{3}{20}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142720 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2210" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142720 #edb/ref 1071 "Use the model below to calculate $\\dfrac{5}{6} \\div 4.$\n\n![](images/d1/d1c1c3842b04174137bfe8a938c70493493b2c9a0e74bee619d965446c9326a6.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142720 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c0f9c9b1-08f9-5ae6-8583-0b7f93904a18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142720 #edb/ref 1074 "Since we need to divide by $\\color{blue}4$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}4$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/24/24bffed596b77ba53d57e04ebb6baede437d40f825c03a794ae7689f11c3c250.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{5}{24}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{6} \\div 4 = \\dfrac{5}{24} \\, .\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142942 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048460 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142942 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186143497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142942 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186143498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142942 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142942 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142942 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142942 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142942 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433944 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142942 #edb/ref 1039 "Interpreting a Division Model" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142942 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186142717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142942 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "489a2e3f-b599-5a48-8957-5f9f452b262e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142943 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186143535 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142943 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186143536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142943 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142943 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142943 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1