#edb/ref 17592186143890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143062 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186143891 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143062 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186143892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143062 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186143893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143062 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186143894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143062 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143062 #edb/ref 1045 "Dividing Fractions by Whole Numbers Using Models" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143062 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186143890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143062 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143062 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143062 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "01f57b72-3b17-525a-9e25-49d9674b599f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143499 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186141963 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143499 #edb/ref 1069 "q-59780" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143499 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143499 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/7f/7f83fbd712fa6864377a93e91c0fc9e50c7bfd3c3a9e176e9dfe30cbb5b978ea.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate $\\frac{2}{3}÷3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143499 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8b1ec8fb-1f41-5fdc-9959-c24d1a3add4d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143499 #edb/ref 1074 "Since we need to divide by $3$, we split the whole into $3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/9b/9bf718ede82077383cd81314c025a1752820e5d39c20cf3b45700e721bd16f3f.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{2}{9}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}÷3=\\frac{2}{9}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143542 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186142221 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143542 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61234" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143542 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143542 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/1b/1bdaebd241576e9101a30d6b8882950494220a2f06f9fdbe1e357107fafabe9e.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the division problem above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143542 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1f89fb8d-4b5b-5292-a64a-e181392d9a34" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143542 #edb/ref 1074 "We have $\\frac{2}{3}$ on the left and $\\frac{2}{12}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/6f/6f6687c4190a54e9974dc600ced3a2662718cce1bcd5d49410a994259ac06e58.png)\n\nThe division operation splits each vertical line into $4$ equal parts. So the shaded parts on the left are $4$ times larger than the shaded parts on the right. \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}÷4=\\frac{2}{12}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143890 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186143891 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143890 #edb/ref 1061 7605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143890 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "467f66f4-545a-520d-bca9-01a2adeee469" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143890 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186144002 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143891 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186143892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143891 #edb/ref 1061 7606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143891 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0539910c-494c-540e-ae2b-8bbc91752500" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143891 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186142942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143892 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186143893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143892 #edb/ref 1061 7607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143892 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6e2d7314-86e8-5702-993e-a914e3f5b75d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143892 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186142943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143893 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186143894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143893 #edb/ref 1061 7608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143893 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f0b9a4cb-e530-53ac-8e4b-9032f1cb3e4f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143893 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186142944 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143894 #edb/ref 1061 7609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143894 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d3624f8d-c0fe-5c69-88ef-4fab2717d2d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143894 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186142945 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144002 #edb/ref 1064 "When we divide a fraction by a whole number, say ${\\color{red}{2}},$ the idea is to \n\n- split the fraction into ${\\color{red}{2}}$ equal parts, and\n\n- determine the fraction that makes up each part.\n\nFor example, suppose we wish to find the value of \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{5} \\div 2.\n$$\n\nLet's start by drawing the fraction model for $\\dfrac45\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/d1/d159ff7e61ae308f27dd561cc8b219f0fc5b5fa46135ebff70ed15558186280b.png)\n\nWe need to divide this fraction by ${\\color{red}{2}}.$ To do this, we draw a horizontal line through our fraction that splits it into $\\color{red}2$ *equal parts*.\n\n![](images/87/87c0a9dad9ab63de7858e8857e412b4d6ce849dfc0b02a172a5debe420c5baf6.png)\n\nWe only need to determine the fraction that makes up one of the parts. Therefore, we can focus on only one row (i.e., the bottom row).\n\nNow, we remove all the shaded parts not in the bottom row. \n\n![](images/54/54a3760d69e7622afa800e4fe107cdafc7069a1fd31138a9ad6c63e8cf6f8f1f.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{4}{10}$ of the whole. Therefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{5} \\div 2 = \\dfrac{4}{10} \\, .\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144002 #edb/ref 1065 2029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144002 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "411e9b60-5c7b-58a3-ba5a-8abc08a8f51a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144002 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433824 #edb/ref 1080 "images/af/af8346a55366c3309e37a8d4ee131d90475688f1657edca8fd4c48dd312bed82.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433824 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175